# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020753> (Orthocoronavirinae infectious disease)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020753> "Infectious disease causes by viruses in the subfamily Orthocoronavirinae (coronaviruses). In humans, coronaviruses cause respiratory tract infections that can be mild, such as some cases of the common cold (among other possible causes, predominantly rhinoviruses), and others that can be lethal, such as SARS, MERS, and COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020753> "Orthocoronavirinae infectious disease")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020753> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005718>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020799> (basal cell neoplasm)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020799> "A neoplastic proliferation of basal cells in the epidermis (part of the skin) or other anatomic sites (most frequently the salivary glands). The basal cell neoplastic proliferation in the epidermis results in basal cell carcinomas. The basal cell neoplastic proliferation in the salivary glands can be benign, resulting in basal cell adenomas or malignant, resulting in basal cell adenocarcinomas.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020799> "neoplasm, basal cell")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020799> "basal cell neoplasm")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0020799> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005626>)

